  "notes": "WRITING:\nAlso written as {茹|ゆ}で{卵|たまご}. The hiragana-kanji mixed form ゆで{卵|たまご} is most common.\n\nTYPES:\n- {半熟|はんじゅく}ゆで{卵|たまご} — soft-boiled egg\n- {固|かた}ゆで{卵|たまご} — hard-boiled egg\n- {味|あじ}{付|つ}きゆで{卵|たまご} — seasoned boiled egg (like {煮卵|にたまご})\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nBoiled eggs are a standard ramen topping ({味玉|あじたま}) and a classic convenience store item in Japan. {温泉卵|おんせんたまご} (hot spring egg) is a related but different preparation.",
